# ── Android APK build (TWA) — shelved ──
#
# The whole android/ tree is kept out of the repository. The APK is not part of
# the work being written up, and carrying a Gradle project, a CI workflow and a
# signing identity for something nobody is shipping is upkeep the paper does not
# owe. Nothing here is deleted: the project still builds from this working copy
# exactly as it did, it is simply not the repository's problem until someone
# decides to ship it. Un-ignore this block to bring it back.
android/

# The signing keystore and its password, listed again on their own so they stay
# ignored even if the line above is ever removed. This key cannot be
# regenerated: the APK's identity to Android IS this key, its SHA-256 is what
# public/.well-known/assetlinks.json pins, and every future update must be
# signed with the same one. Lose it and installed phones cannot be upgraded —
# they must uninstall and reinstall, losing their notification permission with
# it. Back it up somewhere outside this repository, and never commit it: anyone
# holding it can build an APK that Android accepts as TulongGuro.
android/*.keystore
android/*.jks
android/keystore-password.txt

# Builds the APK in CI. No use without the android/ project above.
.github/workflows/android-apk.yml

# How to build, sign and ship the APK. Documents the shelved tree, not the app.
docs/ANDROID-APK.md

# Digital Asset Links — the half of the two-way handshake that the deployed
# site serves so Android trusts the APK to open tulong-guro links without the
# address bar. It pins the keystore fingerprint above, so it means nothing on
# its own and is dead weight on the web deployment while the APK is shelved.
public/.well-known/

# Screenshots attached to a bug report, like /bugs screenshots above.
/gradebook issues

# The per-page cache scripts/crawl-ebeis-masterlist.js writes as it walks the
# EBEIS report — ~2,900 small files. It exists so an interrupted crawl resumes
# instead of restarting, and so a doubted page can be deleted and refetched;
# it rebuilds from the network and is worthless to anyone who did not run the
# crawl. server/data/deped-schools.json is the artefact worth committing.
server/data/ebeis-raw/

# Copies of a previous masterlist kept while replacing it. Same 6 MB as the
# real file, with none of its authority — git history is the right place to
# reach an older one from.
server/data/*-backup.json
/new issues
check.py
check2.py
